      },
      "blocks": {
        "q-1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I really not have to rinse?",
            "answer": "<p>Really. Soak the surface, put the hose away, get on with your weekend. Rain and UV do the follow-up over the coming weeks.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q-2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long until I see results?",
            "answer": "<p>Surface grime starts lifting with the first decent rain. Moss, mould, algae and lichen brown off and weather away over the following weeks — stubborn growth in sheltered spots can take a few months. It's the opposite of instant — that's why it lasts.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q-3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What about my garden, kids and pets?",
            "answer": "<p>There's no acid and no bleach in it — but it's still a serious outdoor cleaner, so treat it with respect. Water surrounding plants and grass before and after you apply, keep the spray off plants and animals, and keep everyone off treated surfaces until they're dry. Full directions are on the label.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q-4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who actually makes this?",
            "answer": "<p>Maximum Wash Ltd — a professional exterior cleaning company with around 20 staff washing buildings across Auckland, Tauranga and Christchurch. Soak n Go is the product we'd use at home.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
